In secure software design, Automata and Computability Theory govern how input parsers, compilers, routing handlers, and web applications process text strings. A web application is essentially a large state machine processing strings. When a developer builds an insecure parser, an unauthenticated user can construct strings that force the parser into unintended states, leading to security flaws.
